,2, cos(2) is negative, so +0*cos(2) is IEEE -0; the independent x oracle preserves that sign. Distinct parameter occurrences are retained; the output must not deduplicate them merely because their coordinates agree.\u000a\u000aMode: execution. Profile: studio-draft. Capability: frog.studio.formula.evaluation@1; compiled owned-value service.\u000aExpected:\u000aoutput-x_values (array<f64>) = [0,0,-0]\u000aoutput-y_values (array<f64>) = [0,0,0]\u000aoutput-error (i32) = 0\u000a","documentation_uri":"","name":"Adaptive polar sampling preserves parameter occurrences","name_source":"document","program_version":"0.0.0.0","tags":["formula","native","typed","independent-oracle","example"]},"storage":{"array_mode":"automatic","version":1},"title":"Adaptive polar sampling preserves parameter occurrences"}
